            "description": "Watch Always Ready vs Lanus highlights and goals from CONMEBOL Libertadores on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on May 6, 2026. The CONMEBOL Libertadores action returned on May 6, 2026, as Always Ready hosted Lanus in a high-stakes encounter. Both teams took to the pitch with clear ambitions, setting the stage for a match filled with intensity and tactical battles in front of an expectant crowd. Early Drama and the Opening Goal The match ignited early when Always Ready was awarded a penalty in the 13th minute. However, the stadium fell into a momentary hush as Fernando Saucedo failed to convert from the spot. The miss did not deter the home side, who continued to apply relentless pressure. Their persistence was rewarded in the 26th minute when Richet Gomez clinicaly finished a pass from Hector Cuellar , breaking the deadlock and shifting the momentum firmly in favor of the hosts. Doubling the Advantage As the first half drew to a close, Always Ready looked to consolidate their lead. Lanus struggled to contain the fluid movement of the opposition and eventually conceded again in the 45th minute. Enrique Triverio found the back of the net after being set up by Carlitos Rodriguez , ensuring the hosts went into the interval with a comfortable two-goal cushion. The visitors attempted to react with tactical substitutions at half-time, bringing on Dylan Aquino , but the challenge ahead remained steep. A Commanding Second Half Finish The restart provided no respite for the visitors. Only a minute into the second half, Joel Amoroso extended the lead to three after an assist from Jesus Maraude , effectively ending the contest as a competitive spectacle. The remainder of the half was characterized by a flurry of substitutions and bookings, with Dieguito Rodriguez , Dario Torrico , and Agustin Medina all seeing yellow as the intensity remained high. In the dying embers of the game, the home side added further gloss to the scoreline. In 