            "description": "Watch Always Ready vs Mirassol highlights and goals from CONMEBOL Libertadores on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on May 19, 2026. High Stakes at the Libertadores On May 19, 2026, the football pitch became a battleground for the CONMEBOL Libertadores as Always Ready hosted Mirassol in a match defined by tactical physicality and shifting momentum. The atmosphere was charged from the opening whistle, with both sides treating every possession as a vital chance to assert dominance in the tournament. Tactical Battles and Early Goals Mirassol drew first blood in the 11th minute when Shaylon capitalized on an assist from Alesson Batista to silence the home crowd. The goal set a frantic tone, with the first half becoming increasingly scrappy as both teams struggled to contain the opposition, leading to a flurry of disciplinary actions. Always Ready worked hard to stabilize, but the visitors entered the break with their slender lead intact. The Dramatic Climax The intensity did not drop in the second half, with the match becoming a test of composure as fouls mounted up. The pressure finally yielded a breakthrough for the hosts in the 75th minute, as Jesus Maraude netted the equalizer after a clever setup by Enrique Triverio . However, the decisive moment arrived at the 82-minute mark when Nathan Fogaca fired home, again assisted by Alesson Batista , to swing the tide back in favor of Mirassol . Despite the late drama of a red card for Victor Luis , the visitors held their ground to secure a hard-fought result.",
