            "description": "Watch Mirassol vs Always Ready highlights and goals from CONMEBOL Libertadores on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on April 29, 2026. Mirassol and Always Ready locked horns in a high-stakes CONMEBOL Libertadores fixture that tested the limits of both sides' tactical discipline and composure. The encounter on April 29, 2026 , provided a rollercoaster of emotions, with the momentum shifting unpredictably as the officiating and clinical finishing took center stage. Early Breakthrough and Physicality The match ignited early under the continental lights as Mirassol wasted no time establishing their presence. In just the 10th minute, a slick attacking move saw Alesson Batista turn provider, threading a precise pass to Carlos Eduardo . The forward made no mistake, firing his effort home to give the home side an early advantage. This opening strike forced Always Ready to rethink their defensive approach, but the game quickly descended into a physical battle rather than a tactical chess match. As the first half progressed, the referee was kept busy by a series of reckless challenges. Fernando Saucedo was the first to enter the book for the visitors, followed closely by the goal-provider Alesson Batista and Richet Gomez . The stop-start nature of the game hindered Always Ready 's attempts to find an equalizer before the interval, as the half concluded with both sides more focused on the physical contest than creative play. Tactical Adjustments and Red Card Drama The second half began with a flurry of activity from the touchline. Always Ready manager looked to inject fresh energy into his squad, introducing Fernando Nava and Dieguito Rodriguez immediately after the break. Mirassol also tinkered with their lineup as the hour mark approached, bringing on Daniel Borges and Carlos Eduardo to maintain their intensity. However, the game took a dramatic and potentially disastrous turn for the hosts in the 75th minute. In a moment of madness that sparked heavy protests from the home bench and players, Joao Victor was shown a straight red card. The dismissal left Mirassol a man down for the final quarter of the match, handing Always Ready a golden opportunity to capitalize on their numerical superiority. The atmosphere grew increasingly hostile as the visitors pushed forward, sensing a chance to salvage a result from the encounter. Clinical Response and Final Whistle Despite the disadvantage, Mirassol demonstrated remarkable resilience. Rather than retreating into a defensive shell, they caught Always Ready off guard with a clinical counter-attack in the 80th minute. In a poetic reversal of the first goal, Carlos Eduardo turned creator, setting up Alesson Batista to double the lead and effectively kill off the contest. The goal stunned the visitors, who had expected to dominate the closing stages against ten men. The final minutes were marked by further disciplinary action as Denilson and Walter were cautioned in a frantic finish. Always Ready threw on Maximo Mamani in a desperate attempt to find a late lifeline, but Mirassol 's organized backline held firm through seven minutes of stoppage time. When the final whistle eventually blew, it confirmed a hard-fought victory for the hosts, who navigated a treacherous second half to secure all three points in their Libertadores campaign.",
